{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a cooperative photoredox and N-heterocyclic carbene (NHC) catalysis method for the regioselective sp2 C-H aroylation of di- and trisubstituted allenes. Using 4CzIPN as a photocatalyst and triazolium-based NHCs, the reaction proceeds via an allene radical cation intermediate that is trapped by a benzoate nucleophile, followed by cross-coupling with an NHC-derived ketyl radical to yield functionalized allenes in good yields.",
